      "narrative": "Mara Venn sets down her copper mug, the liquid inside barely touched. Her sharp eyes hold yours as she leans forward across the scarred table, the charcoal coat rustling.\n\n\"The Ash Gate.\" She says the name like it leaves a bitter taste. \"It was never meant to be a door. It's a wound \u2014 a crack between this world and the Grey, sealed by the Kestrel Guild's pact a hundred years ago. The lock was Toran's work.\" She jerks her chin toward the nervous clerk at the bar."
