      "narrative": "Mara Venn's fingers trace the rim of her mug as she considers your question. She tilts her head slightly, the copper lamplight catching the grey streaks in her dark hair.\n\n\"It wasn't just Toran who had hands on that gate,\" she says, voice dropping low. \"The lock mechanism \u2014 the delicate inner works \u2014 that was his. But the heavy ironwork? The brackets, the hinges, the reinforcing bands?\" She taps the table twice. \"That was Grom's doing. Local blacksmith. Burly man, arms like tree roots. He forged the iron frame that held the whole thing together.\"\n\nHer eyes narrow as she adds, \"And that ironwork was compromised before the gate fell. Someone got to Grom's work \u2014 filed the pins, weakened the brackets from the inside. The question is whether Grom knew about it... or was the one who did it himself.\""
    },
