      "narrative": "The question hangs in the air. Mara Venn's fingers stop their tracing on the mug. She looks at you, then past you, her jaw working.\n\n\"That's...\" She exhales slowly through her nose. \"That's the part I haven't pinned down yet.\"\n\nShe reaches into her coat and pulls out a folded scrap of paper, creased and softened at the edges. She unfolds it, glances at it, then tucks it away again without showing you.\n\n\"I've been chasing the same question for three weeks. Everyone I ask gives me a different name, or no name at all. The Kestrel Guild's records were burned the night the gate was sealed. The ferryman who ran the passage \u2014 Old Bram \u2014 he'd know. He took the coin, he kept the ledger.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes, and there's something raw in her expression. Frustration. Maybe shame.\n\n\"But Bram's dead. Has been for a month. Found him floating face-down in the channel below the gate. The coroner called it a slip. I call it convenient.\"\n\nShe picks up her mug, takes a long drink, and sets it down harder than necessary.\n\n\"So I don't have a name for you, Kael. Not yet. And anyone who claims they do is either lying or fishing for your coin.\""
    },
