      "narrative": "The door of the Copper Finch swings shut behind you, cutting off the tavern's warmth and leaving you in the grey morning air. Rain has slicked the cobblestones to a dark sheen, and the street slopes upward toward the edge of town where the buildings thin and the sky opens wide.\n\nThe Ash Gate rises at the end of the road, a cracked black arch standing alone against the grey sky like a broken tooth. No wall flanks it \u2014 it simply stands there, a doorway to nothing, its ironwork crusted with rust and its surface scarred by what looks like claw marks. The channel Mara mentioned runs beneath it, dark water moving slow and oily between moss-slicked stones.\n\nAs you approach, you notice a figure already there. A courier in a travel-stained cloak stands before the gate, one hand pressed flat against its iron surface as though listening for something on the other side. They don't turn at your approach, but their shoulders stiffen \u2014 they know you're here.\n\nThe air around the gate feels wrong. Thinner. Colder than it should be. The rain seems to avoid the arch itself, falling in a perfect perimeter around its base."
    },
