      "narrative": "The courier's hand drops from the iron surface. They turn slowly, revealing a sharp-featured face beneath the cloak's hood \u2014 young, with watchful eyes the colour of wet slate.\n\n\"Old Bram?\" The courier's voice is flat, almost amused. \"You'll get no answer from him. Not unless you plan to shout into the Grey itself.\"\n\nThey gesture at the dark channel beneath the arch. \"He's in there. Or what's left of him is. Fished him out a month ago, bloated and blue.\"\n\nThe courier \u2014 Sable Quill, you recall Mara mentioning the name \u2014 takes a step closer, boots splashing in a shallow puddle. \"But if you're set on calling, don't let me stop you. Maybe something answers. Just don't expect it to be Bram.\"\n\nThey fold their arms and watch, curiosity glinting beneath the hood's shadow."
    },
