      "narrative": "Kael, you step past the courier and crouch beneath the arch, the cold from the stone seeping through your boots. The ground here is uneven \u2014 cobbles worn smooth by decades of feet and weather, but something catches your eye near the base of the left pillar.\n\nA faint indentation in the stone. Not a crack or a chip \u2014 a deliberate seam, nearly invisible beneath years of grime. You run your fingers along it and feel a slight give. Pressing harder, a section of the stone shifts inward with a grating whisper, revealing a shallow compartment no larger than a bread loaf.\n\nInside rest two vials of glowing blue liquid. The glass is cool to the touch, and the liquid inside pulses with a faint, rhythmic light \u2014 like a slow heartbeat. You notice the dust inside the compartment forms a pattern that doesn't match the settled grime around it. Clean edges, undisturbed corners. Whatever placed these here did so recently. Within the last few days, at most.\n\nSable Quill leans in over your shoulder, their voice losing its flat edge. \"Well now. That's not something you see every day.\""
